= Using the ucs2character class =

* [#intro Introduction]
* [#isxxx Analyzing Characters]
* [#toxxx Transforming Characters]
* [#inset Member of a Set]


[=#intro]
== Introduction ==

The [../classes/html/classucs2character.html ucs2character class] provides static methods for evaluating and manipulating UCS-2 characters.


[=#isxxx]
== Analyzing Characters ==

Methods are provided for determining if a UCS-2 character is alphabetic, alphanumeric, lower case, upper case, etc.

{{{#!blockquote
{{{#!code
@../../examples/ucs2character-isxxx.cpp@
}}}
}}}


[=#toxxx]
== Transforming Characters ==

Methods are also provided for transforming the UCS-2 character to upper or lower case, and to 7-bit ascii, by clearing the higher order bits.

{{{#!blockquote
{{{#!code
@../../examples/ucs2character-toxxx.cpp@
}}}
}}}


[=#inset]
== Member of a Set ==

An isInSet() method is also provided which returns true if the specified UCS-2 character is a member of the specified set of UCS-2 characters and false otherwise.

{{{#!blockquote
{{{#!code
@../../examples/ucs2character-inset.cpp@
}}}
}}}

